{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.joint_action_discharged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.joint_action_discharged","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L81-L104","doc":"**Proposition (`prop:joint-galois-braid-discharged`, conditional on\n[`JointGaloisBraidDecomposition`]).**\n\nThe joint motivic-Galois × braid action commutes on every\nbi-filtration cell:\n`galois g (braid b x) = braid b (galois g x)`.\n\n**Derived — not assumed.** Applying `decomp` to both sides, the\ndisjoint-factor hypotheses `galois_on_A` and `braid_on_B` send each\ncomposite to the single pair `(galoisA g a, braidB b b')` — the\ninterchange law for `galoisA ⊗ id` and `id ⊗ braidB` acting on\ndisjoint coordinates — and injectivity of `decomp` transports the\nequality back to `Cell`. The only unproved input in the chain is the\nclass instance for the concrete `𝓗_q^{(n,K)}` (left unbuilt). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:joint-galois-braid-discharged","label":"prop:joint-galois-braid-discharged","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/joint-galois-braid-discharged.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.braid_on_B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.braid_on_B","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L78-L78","doc":"**Disjointness hypothesis (braid ↦ B-factor).** Under the\ndecomposition the braid action is `id ⊗ braidB`: it moves the\n`B`-coordinate and fixes the `A`-coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.galois_on_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.galois_on_A","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L73-L73","doc":"**Disjointness hypothesis (Galois ↦ A-factor).** Under the\ndecomposition the Galois action is `galoisA ⊗ id`: it moves the\n`A`-coordinate and fixes the `B`-coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.braidB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.braidB","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The braid action restricted to the right factor `B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.galoisA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.galoisA","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The motivic-Galois action restricted to the left factor `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.braid","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The braid action on the whole cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.galois","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.galois","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The motivic-Galois action on the whole cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.decomp_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.decomp_inj","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L61-L61","doc":"A tensor iso is injective on underlying sets: the decomposition\nseparates points of the cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.decomp","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The disjoint tensor decomposition `Cell ↪ A ⊗ B`\n(underlying-set image of the categorical iso). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.BraidAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.BraidAction","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Braid group elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.GaloisAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.GaloisAction","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Motivic-Galois group elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.B","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Right tensor factor — the braid action sees only this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.A","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Left tensor factor — the motivic-Galois action sees only this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.Cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.Cell","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The bi-filtration cell carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidDischarged.JointGaloisBraidDecomposition","kind":"class","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidDischarged.lean#L31-L79","doc":"**Conditional-class hypotheses for `prop:joint-galois-braid-discharged`.**\n\nEncodes the manuscript's *structural input* (not its conclusion): the\nbi-filtration cell splits as a disjoint tensor product `Cell ≅ A ⊗ B`\n(here modeled at the underlying-set level as an injection\n`decomp : Cell → A × B`), the motivic-Galois action moves only the `A`\nfactor (`galois = galoisA ⊗ id`), and the braid action moves only the\n`B` factor (`braid = id ⊗ braidB`).\n\nThe fields are genuine hypotheses — the disjoint-factor intertwining\nequations — from which commutation is *derived* in\n`joint_action_discharged`, never assumed. In particular there is no\nfield asserting \"galois commutes with every function\"; that would be\nthe conclusion in disguise. ","signatureChunk":0}]}